@startuml proposal-implementation-issue-states
' cumin works - PROPOSAL, not the rule of today: states of an implementation issue, as they could be.
' Differences from today are marked NEW. See the draft pull request for the reasons.
' Every activity, guard, and effect names who acts: cumin, the Implementer, the Reviewer, or the Owner.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / the Planner or the Owner writes the issue

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits for a free slot

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the Implementer works

state "awaiting-checks" as Checks
Checks : do / GitHub runs the required checks

state "reviewing" as Reviewing
Reviewing : do / the Reviewer reviews the pull request

state "awaiting-merge-decision  (NEW name)" as OwnerReview
OwnerReview : do / the Owner reviews the pull request

state "merging  (NEW state)" as Merging
Merging : do / cumin merges the pull request,\nthen closes the issue

state "awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Owner answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Ready --> Implementing : [the Owner added ready, the blockers are closed,\ncumin has a free slot]\n/ cumin requests the implementation\nfrom the Implementer
Implementing --> Checks : [no Implementer runs, cumin verified\nthe pull request]\n/ cumin adds the closing link
Implementing --> Implementing : [no Implementer runs, cumin found no\nverified pull request, first time]\n/ cumin requests the Implementer again  (NEW)
Implementing --> Decision : [no Implementer runs, and: the Implementer\nasked a question, or it is the second time]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Checks --> Reviewing : [the required checks passed]\n/ cumin requests the review from the Reviewer
Checks --> Implementing : [a required check failed, cumin's fix\nrequests are under the limit]\n/ cumin requests a check fix from the Implementer
Checks --> Decision : [a required check failed and the fix requests\nare at the limit; or a check gave no result in time]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Checks --> Implementing : [the pull request conflicts]\n/ cumin requests a conflict resolution\nfrom the Implementer
Reviewing --> Implementing : [no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer requested changes\non the head commit, the rounds are under the limit]\n/ cumin requests a review fix from the Implementer
Reviewing --> Merging : [no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer approved the\nhead commit, the checks passed, risk/low]\n/ cumin changes the label  (NEW target)
Reviewing --> OwnerReview : [no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer approved the\nhead commit, the checks passed,\nrisk/medium or risk/high]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Reviewing --> Checks : [no Reviewer runs, and: the Implementer or the Owner\nmoved the head commit, or a check does not pass]\n/ cumin changes the label
Reviewing --> Reviewing : [no Reviewer runs, the Reviewer left no review\non the head commit, first time]\n/ cumin requests the review again
Reviewing --> Decision : [no Reviewer runs, and: the rounds are at the limit,\nthe Reviewer asked a question, or it is the second time]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
OwnerReview --> Merging : [the Owner approved the head commit,\nthe checks passed]\n/ cumin changes the label  (NEW target)
OwnerReview --> Implementing : [the Owner requested changes]\n/ cumin requests a response from the Implementer
OwnerReview --> Implementing : [the pull request conflicts]\n/ cumin requests a conflict resolution\nfrom the Implementer
OwnerReview --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Merging --> [*] : [GitHub shows the pull request as merged]\n/ cumin closes the issue and writes\nthe follow-up note
Merging --> Implementing : [GitHub refused the merge: conflict]\n/ cumin requests a conflict resolution\nfrom the Implementer
Merging --> Decision : [GitHub refused the merge for another\nlasting reason]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Decision --> Ready : the Owner adds ready

legend right
  PROPOSAL. A box is a state: a label on GitHub (written without "cumin/status/").
  "do /" says who works in the state. An arrow is: trigger [guard] / effect, each with its actor.
  Every guard reads only facts on GitHub and "no agent runs for this issue".
  No arrow needs the event "the run ended": a restart of cumin loses nothing.
  "merging" makes a merge whose answer was lost visible: the next poll reads whether the pull request is merged.
endlegend

@enduml
